# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for holder-core.
#
# Use with: TSAN_OPTIONS="suppressions=<path>/tests/tsan.supp" ./holder_core_tests
#
# These are pre-existing, out-of-scope concurrency limitations -- not defects in
# the RealGitOps ownership / per-project locking change. They belong to the
# planned broad "make holder-core safe to call concurrently" audit.

# git_signature_now() -> localtime()/tzset() mutates glibc's process-global
# timezone state (tzname/timezone/daylight) without synchronization. Two threads
# creating commits in *different* projects at the same time race here. The
# per-project lock intentionally does not serialize different projects, so this
# is visible; the real fixes (call tzset() once at startup, pin the signature
# time zone, or serialize signature creation) are a behavioural decision left to
# the concurrency audit.
race:tzset_internal
called_from_lib:libgit2.so
